[Music]  it's been eight  months since the gang rape and killing  of a 19 year old girl in the state of  uttar pradesh  like many journalists siddhi kapan was  trying to report on the incident in the  district of hatras  when he was arrested and held in jail  accused of sedition  his family in the state of kerala say  kapan who's the general secretary of a  union of journalists  was only doing his job  it's our 19th wedding anniversary in  july i've known him for a long time now  i very well know what kind of person he  is the only mistake he made was to  travel with a member of an islamist  organization  as the uttar pradesh government faced  mountain criticism for its handling of  the case  police charged kapan and 21 others under  a law from the british colonial era  researchers say sedition is meant to be  used only against those who try to  overthrow the government by force  but there's been a reported 28 increase  in the use of the charge  every year since prime minister narendra  modi came to power in 2014.  the minister of state for home affairs  has previously said  cases under the law are not unique to  the government of narendra modi and  their numbers are low  most of those charged protesters  students academics journalists  and opposition politicians i suppose the  current government doesn't  like uh anyone disagreeing with it or  criticizing it for its measures and it  prefers to come down on that with a very  heavy  response rather than engaging in a very  you know peaceful dialogue with someone  who's criticizing them  one senior lawyer has been petitioning  the supreme court to get rid of the law  there's no justification for this law to  remain in the statute books  because incitement to violence or  incitement to public disorder  our offenses in any case under different  sections of the penal code  so this is totally redundant this law  was brought by the british government  to prevent any criticism of the british  government by the  indian subjects in that colonial times  so it has no relevance today  those campaigning against misuse of the  law were recently given some hope by  india's top court  last week the supreme court threw out a  case against a senior journalist who  criticized the government  saying disapproval doesn't amount to  sedition  the judgment is being seen as the court  pushing back against a high  number of cases being brought under that  charge  reinert says she hopes this means kapan  will be released from  jail soon elizabeth paranam al jazeera  new delhi

